---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PUBLISHER, SITE } from '../consts';
import { simplePageBreadcrumb } from '../lib/schema';

const description = `Privacy Policy for ${SITE.name}.com. Learn how we collect, use, and protect your information, our use of cookies, Google AdSense, DoubleClick DART cookies, and your rights under GDPR and CCPA.`;
const url = `${SITE.url}/cookies-privacy-policy/`;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy"
      {description} canonical={url} schema={[
        {
          '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `${url}#webpage`, url,
          name: 'Privacy Policy', description,
          isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
        },
        simplePageBreadcrumb('/cookies-privacy-policy/', 'Privacy Policy'),
      ]}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</nav>
    <div class="prose" style="padding:34px 0 10px">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 2 October 2026. Effective date: 2 October 2026.</p>

      <p>
        At <strong>{SITE.name}.com</strong> ("{SITE.name}", "we", "us", or "our"), accessible from <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a>, the privacy of our visitors is of paramount importance to us. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of personal information that is received and collected by {SITE.name}.com and how it is used, stored, and safeguarded.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Data Controller Information</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name}.com is owned and operated by <strong>{PUBLISHER.legalName}</strong>, a {PUBLISHER.companyType.toLowerCase()} registered in {PUBLISHER.jurisdiction} under company number {PUBLISHER.companyNumber}, with its registered office located at:
      </p>
      <p>
        {PUBLISHER.legalName}<br />
        {PUBLISHER.address.street}<br />
        {PUBLISHER.address.city}, {PUBLISHER.address.postcode}<br />
        {PUBLISHER.address.country}
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or your personal data, please contact our Data Protection desk via email at <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a> or <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.contactEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
      <h3>Log Files and Technical Data</h3>
      <p>
        Like most standard website servers, {SITE.name}.com utilizes log files to maintain server integrity, analyze overall traffic trends, and secure the network against malicious traffic. The information inside the log files includes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Internet Protocol (IP) addresses</li>
        <li>Browser type and version</li>
        <li>Internet Service Provider (ISP)</li>
        <li>Date and time stamps</li>
        <li>Referring and exit pages</li>
        <li>Platform / operating system type</li>
        <li>Number of clicks and navigational movement</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This technical information is not linked to any personally identifiable information and is used exclusively for systems administration, diagnostic troubleshooting, and protecting the security and performance of our infrastructure.
      </p>

      <h3>Information You Provide Voluntarily</h3>
      <p>
        Visitors may choose to submit personal data voluntarily through several interactions:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email Inquiries:</strong> When you contact our editorial desk or support team via email (<a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.contactEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.contactEmail}</a> or <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}</a>), we collect your name, email address, and the contents of your message. We process this information under our legitimate interest to respond to your inquiry and retain correspondence records for up to 24 months.</li>
        <li><strong>Newsletter Subscriptions:</strong> If you elect to subscribe to our optional email newsletter, we collect your email address with your explicit affirmative consent. You may withdraw your consent and unsubscribe at any time using the one-click unsubscribe link provided in every newsletter dispatch.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not require user account registration, we do not host public unmoderated user comments, and we do not request or store consumer payment card credentials on {SITE.name}.com.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Cookies and Web Beacons</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name}.com uses cookies to store information about visitors' preferences, to record user-specific information on which pages the site visitor accesses or visits, and to customize our web page content based upon visitors' browser type or other information that the visitor sends via their browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        A cookie is a small text file placed on your device by a web server. You can choose to disable cookies through your individual browser options. Detailed information about cookie management with specific web browsers can be found at the browsers' respective websites. For a complete breakdown of cookies used on our site, please consult our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third-Party Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
      <p>
        Third-party ad servers or ad networks use technologies like cookies, JavaScript, or Web Beacons that are used in their respective advertisements and links that appear on {SITE.name}.com, which are sent directly to your browser. They automatically receive your IP address when this occurs. These technologies are used to measure the effectiveness of their advertising campaigns and/or to personalize the advertising content that you see on websites that you visit.
      </p>
      <p>
        {SITE.name}.com has no access to or control over these cookies that are used by third-party advertisers.
      </p>

      <h3>Google AdSense and the DoubleClick DART Cookie</h3>
      <p>
        Google is one of our primary third-party advertising vendors on {SITE.name}.com. Please note the following regarding Google's advertising practices:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Third-Party Vendors:</strong> Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to {SITE.name}.com or other websites on the Internet.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>DoubleClick DART Cookie:</strong> Google's use of advertising cookies (including the DoubleClick DART cookie) enables it and its partners to serve targeted advertisements to our visitors based on their visit to {SITE.name}.com and/or other websites across the World Wide Web.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Non-Personally Identifiable Information:</strong> The DART cookie tracks browse sessions using non-personally identifiable technical signals and does not collect personal identifiers such as your legal name, physical address, email address, or telephone number.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>How to Opt Out of Personalized Advertising</h3>
      <p>
        You have the explicit right to opt out of personalized interest-based advertising at any time through the following mechanisms:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Ads Settings:</strong> Visitors may opt out of personalized advertising from Google by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings (https://adssettings.google.com/)</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Network Advertising Initiative (NAI):</strong> You may opt out of third-party vendor use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting the <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Network Advertising Initiative Opt-Out Page (https://optout.networkadvertising.org/)</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Digital Advertising Alliance (DAA):</strong> You can manage interest-based ad preferences across participating advertising networks via the <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">DAA WebChoices Tool (https://optout.aboutads.info/)</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>European Interactive Digital Advertising Alliance (EDAA):</strong> European visitors can manage preferences via <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Your Online Choices (https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/)</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. European Economic Area (EEA), UK &amp; Swiss Consent (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h2>
      <p>
        For users visiting from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, {SITE.name}.com complies with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and UK GDPR.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where required by applicable law, we deploy a Google-certified Consent Management Platform (CMP) that integrates with the IAB Europe Transparency and Consent Framework (TCF v2.2). Non-essential cookies and personalized advertising tags remain inactive until you grant your affirmative, informed consent. You can modify or revoke your consent preferences at any time through the consent settings provided on our site.
      </p>
      <p>Under GDPR and UK GDPR, you possess the following rights:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Right of Access:</strong> You have the right to request copies of your personal data held by us.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> You have the right to request that we correct any information you believe is inaccurate or incomplete.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Erasure ("Right to be Forgotten"):</strong> You have the right to request that we erase your personal data under certain conditions.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Restrict Processing:</strong> You have the right to request that we restrict the processing of your personal data under certain conditions.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Object to Processing:</strong> You have the right to object to our processing of your personal data under certain conditions.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Data Portability:</strong> You have the right to request that we transfer the data that we have collected to another organization or directly to you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these rights, please contact our Data Protection Officer at <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a>. We respond to all verified statutory requests within one calendar month. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. California Consumer Privacy Rights (CCPA / CPRA)</h2>
      <p>
        If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), affords you specific rights regarding your personal information:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Right to Know:</strong> You may request disclosure of the categories and specific pieces of personal information collected about you over the preceding 12 months.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> You may request the deletion of personal information collected from you, subject to legal exceptions.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Correct:</strong> You may request correction of inaccurate personal information maintained about you.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Opt Out of Sale or Sharing:</strong> We do not sell personal information in exchange for monetary consideration. However, the use of third-party advertising cookies may be classified as "sharing" under California law. You may opt out of third-party cookie sharing via our consent controls or through the opt-out links detailed in Section 4.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> We will not discriminate against you for exercising any of your CCPA/CPRA rights.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        California consumers may submit a verifiable consumer request by emailing <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a> with "California Privacy Request" in the subject line.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Affiliate Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name}.com participates in affiliate marketing programs. Some of our editorial articles may include affiliate tracking links to hardware accessories, audio devices, or App Store utilities. If you click on an affiliate link and complete a purchase, {SITE.name}.com may receive a small commission at no additional cost to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Affiliate relationships never dictate our technical evaluations, scoring, or editorial opinions. Every article containing affiliate links includes a conspicuous disclosure banner at the top of the post.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA)</h2>
      <p>
        Protecting the privacy of young children is especially important. {SITE.name}.com is a general audience technology publication and does not knowingly collect any personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13.
      </p>
      <p>
        If a parent or guardian believes that {SITE.name}.com has personally identifiable information of a child under the age of 13 in its database, please contact us immediately at <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a> or <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.contactEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.contactEmail}</a>, and we will use our best efforts to promptly remove such information from our records.
      </p>

      <h2>9. External Links to Third-Party Sites</h2>
      <p>
        Our articles contain hyperlinks to third-party websites, including official Apple developer documentation, App Store listings, open-source repositories, and external tech publications. We have no control over the privacy practices, content, or policies of third-party websites. We strongly encourage visitors to review the privacy policies of any third-party websites they choose to visit.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Updates and Consent</h2>
      <p>
        By using our website, you hereby consent to our Privacy Policy and agree to its terms. We reserve the right to revise or update this policy as technical, legal, or regulatory requirements evolve. Any modifications will be posted directly to this page with an updated "Last updated" date.
      </p>
      <p>
        For further inquiries regarding our data practices, please write to us at <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
